WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.269
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:15.263
Unit twenty-two: Water Security. Today you will give conditions with 'unless' and 'as long as'.

4
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:18.146
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.240
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:24.293
Water security.

7
00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:27.875
Water security means having enough safe water.

8
00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:30.912
Water security is a global concern.

9
00:00:31.517 --> 00:00:34.529
Your turn. Say: Water security.

10
00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.867
Water security.

11
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:40.328
Drought.

12
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:43.688
Drought means a long time without rain.

13
00:00:44.283 --> 00:00:46.062
The drought destroyed the rice crop.

14
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.850
Your turn. Say: Drought.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.422
Drought.

16
00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:54.254
Shortage.

17
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.180
Shortage means not having enough.

18
00:00:57.783 --> 00:00:59.806
There is a water shortage in summer.

19
00:01:00.417 --> 00:01:03.092
Your turn. Say: Shortage.

20
00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:06.830
Shortage.

21
00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:08.805
Sanitation.

22
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:13.267
Sanitation means clean toilets and waste systems.

23
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:16.127
Good sanitation prevents disease.

24
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:19.137
Your turn. Say: Sanitation.

25
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.315
Sanitation.

26
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.074
Recycling.

27
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:28.408
Recycling means using something again.

28
00:01:29.017 --> 00:01:31.283
Water recycling helps farms.

29
00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:34.385
Your turn. Say: Recycling.

30
00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:38.292
Recycling.

31
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.272
Conservation.

32
00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:44.281
Conservation means protecting and saving resources.

33
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.231
Water conservation starts at home.

34
00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:50.736
Your turn. Say: Conservation.

35
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.822
Conservation.

36
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:56.666
Rainwater.

37
00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.533
Rainwater means water from rain.

38
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.475
We collect rainwater in big jars.

39
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:05.631
Your turn. Say: Rainwater.

40
00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.700
Rainwater.

41
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.556
Access.

42
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.304
Access means the ability to get or use something.

43
00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:18.659
Every child needs access to clean water.

44
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.798
Your turn. Say: Access.

45
00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:25.820
Access.

46
00:02:26.633 --> 00:02:30.122
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.273
Visal, will we always have enough water?

48
00:02:34.383 --> 00:02:37.393
We will have enough water as long as we save it.

49
00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:39.682
And if we don't?

50
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:44.908
Unless we stop wasting water, there will be shortages.

51
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:47.796
What does your village do?

52
00:02:48.883 --> 00:02:54.670
We collect rainwater. As long as it rains in the wet season, we have water all year.

53
00:02:55.833 --> 00:02:57.310
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.881
Grammar focus: Unless and as long as.

55
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.287
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:05.598
We will have enough water as long as we save it.

57
00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:10.027
Unless we stop wasting water, there will be shortages.

58
00:03:10.917 --> 00:03:13.508
Crops will grow as long as farmers have water.

59
00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:20.013
'As long as' means 'only if'. 'Unless' means 'if not'. Use the present simple after both.

60
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.225
Be careful! Don't say: We will have water as long as we will save it.

61
00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:30.258
Say: We will have water as long as we save it.

62
00:03:30.558 --> 00:03:32.894
Use the present simple after 'as long as'.

63
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.271
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.451
Every Drop Counts.

65
00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.598
Water security means safe water for everyone.

66
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.983
Droughts and shortages are growing problems.

67
00:03:45.967 --> 00:03:48.489
We will have enough water as long as we save it.

68
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.626
Unless we improve sanitation, diseases will spread.

69
00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.678
Rainwater collection and recycling help communities.

70
00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:01.710
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.863
We'll be fine as long as we blank water.

72
00:04:05.163 --> 00:04:09.049
A, save. B, will save. C, saved.

73
00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.356
The answer is A: save.

74
00:04:15.517 --> 00:04:17.876
A long time without rain is a blank.

75
00:04:18.176 --> 00:04:21.330
A, drought. B, shortage. C, flood.

76
00:04:24.867 --> 00:04:26.727
The answer is A: drought.

77
00:04:27.883 --> 00:04:30.359
Clean toilets and waste systems are blank.

78
00:04:30.659 --> 00:04:34.777
A, sanitation. B, conservation. C, access.

79
00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:40.426
The answer is A: sanitation.

80
00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:44.936
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:45.783 --> 00:04:48.538
How can communities improve water security?

82
00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.862
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:59.162 --> 00:05:10.104
Communities can collect rainwater and fix leaking pipes. As long as everyone saves water, we will have enough, but unless we act, shortages will grow.

84
00:05:10.404 --> 00:05:12.032
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:12.917 --> 00:05:17.415
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and unless and as long as.

86
00:05:17.715 --> 00:05:22.794
Today's value is sustainability. Choose ways of living that protect the planet for the future.

87
00:05:23.094 --> 00:05:26.884
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

88
00:05:27.184 --> 00:05:30.103
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

